            <Placemark id="2652">
                <name>Pera Palace </name>
                <description>
                category  : Sleep_Splurge &lt;br&gt;
                address  : Meşrutiyet Cd 52  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://perapalace.com  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Opened in 1892 and sitting on a hill overlooking the Golden Horn. They make much of their history, and a stellar cast of celebs have stayed here, including Agatha Christie. They claim she wrote ''Murder on the Orient Express'' in room 411, though she probably wrote the first draft in Arpachiyah in Iraq. Atatürk often used Room 101 in the early days of the Republic, and that's now a museum. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
