            <Placemark id="2690">
                <name>Edirne</name>
                <description>
                category  : Go next_West &lt;br&gt;
                address  :  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Edirne, two hours to the northwest, is a beautiful historic city, and was the Ottoman capital before power moved to Istanbul. You need at least a day here. A slow scenic route winds north via Kıyıköy, ancient Medea, a fisherman's village on the Black Sea with some traditional architecture, partially rebuilt ancient city walls and a nearby rock-cut monastery. The next town on that route is Vize, an old town with a well preserved Byzantine cathedral. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#170</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2689">
                    <coordinates>26.5587225,41.6759327,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="2692">
                <name>Sofia</name>
                <description>
                category  : Go next_West &lt;br&gt;
                address  :  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Head into Western Europe either via Sofia in Bulgaria or Bucharest in Romania. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#170</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2691">
                    <coordinates>23.3217359,42.6977028,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="2694">
                <name>Via Egnatia</name>
                <description>
                category  : Go next_West &lt;br&gt;
                address  :  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Or perhaps you can follow the ancient Via Egnatia all the way to the Adriatic and across to Rome. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#170</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2693">
                    <coordinates>16.8861634,41.118499,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="2696">
                <name>Marmara Islands</name>
                <description>
                category  : Go next_South &lt;br&gt;
                address  :  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : The Marmara Islands are across the sea, much further away and less urban than the Princes Islands just offshore of the city. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#170</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2695">
                    <coordinates>27.6294272,40.6216407,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="2698">
                <name>Bursa</name>
                <description>
                category  : Go next_South &lt;br&gt;
                address  :  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Bursa to the southeast is a former Ottoman capital with many historical sights plus Uludağ|Uludağ National Park just south. İznik, rich in Byzantine, Seljuk, and early Ottoman heritage, is worth a detour on the way. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#170</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2697">
                    <coordinates>28.8944669,39.9895878,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="2700">
                <name>Izmir</name>
                <description>
                category  : Go next_South &lt;br&gt;
                address  :  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : A scenic route towards Izmir is to head west then south into the Gallipoli peninsula, with its World War I sites, cross the Dardanelles to Çanakkale, then past ancient Troy (Turkey)|Troy and Bergama|Pergamon (Bergama). A short ferry-ride brings you to the charming island of Bozcaada. For more detailed descriptions, see Istanbul to Izmir. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#170</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2699">
                    <coordinates>27.02997,38.23166,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
